      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Error log patterns**\n\n- worker_connections are not enough or too many open files: Nginx itself is the bottleneck. Raise worker_connections or the descriptor limits, and relate it to the Node.js WebSocket connections.\n- upstream timed out or connection refused: the problem is in the backend, not Nginx.\n- no live upstreams: every instance failed its health checks, which is a full outage (SLI-1 collapses).\n- limiting requests: rate limiting is working. A large count can mean an attack or an overly strict limit.\n- Nothing: no limit or failure was hit.\n\n"
      }
    },
